---\nG0 CONFIG ATTESTATION. Record repo URL + commit, full CLI, resolved config dump,\n   driver/CUDA/framework versions, topology (nvidia-smi topo -m), pinned clocks.\n   The scheduler must log the pending-wgrad budget it actually adopted (after\n   parsing/clamping) and the max pending count observed at runtime.\nG1 FLAG-SENSITIVITY GATE (C4) - FIRST SUBSTANTIVE GATE.\n   Sweep D = --zero-bubble-max-pending-backward in {1, p, 2p-1, 2p, 4p} at fixed\n   (p, m, model). Require (i) runtime-observed pending count tracks D, (ii)\n   makespan monotone non-increasing in D, (iii) the per-stage Gantt actually\n   changes.\n   OUTCOME A: no change at all (even 1 vs p) and observed pending does not track\n     D -> flag ignored or clamped. VERDICT \"precondition not met\"; no near-zero\n     claim admissible; the answer is NOT \"bubble not measured\" but \"premise\n     failed\".\n   OUTCOME B: visible change below some D*, but 2p-1 == 2p == 4p -> saturation;\n     \"2p\" is over-provisioning; report the claim at the saturation point and say\n     so. [OFFLINE REF] With uniform costs the reference saturates at D = p:\n     makespan identical for D in {p, 2p-1, 2p, 4p} (p=8,m=32 -> 103) while peak\n     held inputs grow 22 -> 30 -> 32. So D=2p may buy only memory. To be\n     falsified on real hardware; a first-order \"in practice\" result either way.\nG2 INSTRUMENT VALIDITY GATE (hard).\n   C1 positive control: the same instrument on 1F1B must reproduce the analytic\n   bubble (p-1)/(m+p-1) within tolerance. An instrument that cannot measure a\n   KNOWN non-zero bubble cannot certify a near-zero one.\n   C2 noise floor: p=1 single-GPU run + >= 5 repeats of an identical config.\n   C6 instrumentation overhead: profile-on vs profile-off makespan < 2%.\n   C5 work conservation: kernel count / FLOPs / parameter count / loss and\n   grad-norm parity vs 1F1B at identical global batch.\nG3 MEMORY-VALIDITY GATE (primary, not ancillary).\n   Peak allocated/reserved per stage, observed pending-wgrad residency, recompute\n   events, OOM/retry/fallback, any silent micro-batch change. ANY of: micro-batch\n   shrunk, activation recompute introduced, OOM fallback, or residency\n   inconsistent with D  ==>  the measurement is VOID for the near-zero claim and\n   is reported separately as the memory-limited regime (never pooled with valid\n   runs). Retaining up to 2p-1 sets of inputs for deferred wgrad is the most\n   likely mechanism turning a theoretically near-zero bubble into a practically\n   non-zero one.\nG4 METRIC-CONSISTENCY GATE. The ideal-bound metric normalises stage-load\n   imbalance away. [OFFLINE REF] With edge stages 50% heavier (embedding / final\n   loss) bound-bubble = 0.9% (\"near zero\") while aggregate GPU idle = 25.7%, and\n   gap attribution still calls the idle \"waiting on dependency\", i.e.\n   irreducible-LOOKING. A claim is admissible only if |agg_idle - bound_bubble|\n   <= 1 point AND busy_max/busy_mean <= 1.05 (or the imbalance is explicitly\n   modelled, e.g. balanced virtual pipeline).\nG5 H1 DECISION: fwd_idle_rate vs the pre-registered threshold (section 5), by\n   TOST equivalence, at every (p, m/p) cell that passed G1-G4.\nG6 H2 DECISION: irreducible share of idle >= 80% AND bubble x m converges to the\n   fill/drain constant of the cost model [OFFLINE REF: m x bubble -> (p-1)/3 for\n   uniform f=a=w, within 2-3.5% at the largest three m].\nG7 PRACTICALITY: tokens/s/GPU, MFU, speedup vs 1F1B and vs DualPipe at equal\n   global batch and equal memory budget.\nEOF\nwc -c /workspace/l0_sim/DESIGN.md", "exit_code": 0, "timed_out": false, "elapsed_seconds": 0.065, "output": "7003 /workspace/l0_sim/DESIGN.md\n", "output_truncated": false}"}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "0a20f1ae-4ecc-400f-a654-13471409c029", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent"}
